# §13d G2–G4 statement gate: cut checks and landed forms

Tool: `bash <S>/tools/leanelab.sh <OUT>/base <S>/oleans-lb6 <file>` (direct `lean`, no `-o`, no olean
written). Base: <OUT>/base, a read-only `git archive` export of f2d48ad5 (the local
`origin/complexity/arora-barak-ch3-4`; its Lean files equal 1b6b972c's: PRs #92 and #93 merged); its `.lake` is
a symlink to <S>/wt-g24's packages (same `lake-manifest.json`). Snapshot: `oleans-lb6`. Toolchain:
`leanprover/lean4:v4.25.0`. <OUT> is the gate's output directory; <S> the scratchpad. Run: 2026-10-14 18:28 UTC.

`python3 -I <OUT>/scripts/cutcheck.py <OUT>/G24Statements.lean <OUT>/base <OUT>/cut` (the C1 and
stage-2 gates' script, verbatim) writes, for each part, a file holding the imports of the part's import
closure and the bodies of the parts in that closure, in file order. Each is elaborated on its own.
